# Searchlight: turns a cone of light on the nearest enemy unit in range. Every enemy in the cone is solid (as in a
# lantern field) and burns. It draws light only while it shines ("Searchlight light/s").
# Spawned origin 2.0 above ground.
# SHAPE (a placeholder; uniform scales of the baseshapes variants): a dark IRON MAST on a foot (the root) - a thin post
# of two pieces (1.8 m each, overlapping by 0.1 m), a lamp deck turned 45 degrees, the LAMP HEAD 5.4 m over the ground
# and a roof over it. It reads against the Light tower's pale stone obelisk with its blue crystal. The child pieces are
# render-only; the collider is the 4x4x4 m box.
# THE HEAD turns with the cone (StructureSystem::poseAimHeads, from the component's yaw): its local +X is the aim. A dark
# iron LAMP HOUSING (a box and a smaller back cap), a glowing warm LENS face on its front (the `eyes` container: unlit, so
# it glows), and the main crystal seated in the lens, its point out along +X. A small crystal sits on the roof. The cone
# itself is a spot light the game adds each frame from the lamp (keep the `Head` height in step with c_searchlightLamp in
# Game/Private/Light.cpp; the light starts at the lens face, c_searchlightLampClear there). The deck and the roof are
# narrow on purpose: the cone must clear them (the lens and the crystals are unlit pieces with no ray tracing: they cast
# no shadow).
Prefab gameSearchlight
	Global true
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer baseshapes
		Node CubeHalf
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.22 0.23 0.27
		Position 0 -1.3 0
		Scale 1.4
	Component Physics
		Body Static
		ContactEvents true
		Shape Box
		HalfExtents 2 2 2
	Component GameStructure
		AlwaysShowResources true
		MeleeRadius 2
